{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"567486400c732910","type":"group","x":-320,"y":360,"width":760,"height":1600,"label":"THIS SECTION MAY NEED ADJUSTMENTS"},
		{"id":"c9a9286cc20655b3","type":"text","text":"[[Nishi Tsukanda]] starts looking for possible venues to use to support his son's fighting career :3","x":1680,"y":5880,"width":250,"height":160},
		{"id":"5946f82fb491fb9a","type":"text","text":"A drunk [[Marcus Caecor]] approaches [[Nishi Tsukanda|Nishi's Codename]], offering to join Nishi's whole soul magic research thing. Nishi refuses to let him join, and [[Marcus Caecor]] returns home even more depressed.","x":953,"y":6160,"width":360,"height":178},
		{"id":"7d8bf6c0bfa41bce","type":"text","text":"[[Orobi Tsukanda]] loses to [[Orobi's Bestie]] in a fight, and upon reviving has his eye restored.","x":1680,"y":6800,"width":250,"height":161},
		{"id":"490dde8ca6b8107b","type":"text","text":"[[Marcus Caecor]] and [[Nishi Tsukanda]] ultimately come to an agreement related to the use of [[Caecor Arena]].","x":953,"y":6632,"width":360,"height":118},
		{"id":"2f463767b295541f","type":"text","text":"[[Nishi Tsukanda]] shows up at [[Marcus Caecor]]'s apartment and basically starts forcing him to get his shit together.","x":953,"y":6440,"width":360,"height":120},
		{"id":"5b1b4a92b7d906bd","type":"text","text":"[[Mechanical Dragon's Creator]] leaves [[Cyberron]]","x":1900,"y":-4900,"width":360,"height":60},
		{"id":"55469f617574a893","type":"text","text":"[[Mechanical Dragon's Creator]] visits [[Cyberron]]","x":1900,"y":-5320,"width":360,"height":58},
		{"id":"fe229f061e378b35","type":"text","text":"[[Mechanical Dragon's Creator]] builds [[Sakishi Yamanaka]]","x":1900,"y":-5200,"width":360,"height":58},
		{"id":"fc09a5b5de2c6c32","type":"text","text":"[[Mechanical Dragon's Creator]] builds [[Nishi Tsukanda]]","x":1620,"y":-5060,"width":360,"height":60},
		{"id":"005e6260a42f1273","type":"text","text":"[[Sakishi Yamanaka]] builds [[Suuna Yamanaka]]","x":2160,"y":-5060,"width":360,"height":60},
		{"id":"467d645597ca95c3","type":"text","text":"say gex or whatever. will come back to this","x":953,"y":8040,"width":360,"height":80},
		{"id":"0d282fbce57b457a","type":"text","text":"# Dracon Incident/Babyllis War\n\n[[Dr. Sanguis]] works as a field medic?","x":-137,"y":-580,"width":361,"height":214},
		{"id":"aa42664d85dd4302","type":"text","text":"# CALAMITY","x":880,"y":-513,"width":300,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"41a6051e9fb63430","type":"text","text":"# POST CALAMITY\n\n[[Nishi Tsukanda]] builds [[Orobi Tsukanda]].","x":1680,"y":-160,"width":250,"height":192},
		{"id":"b0a17df6786a1468","type":"text","text":"[[Dr. Sanguis]] is hired by [[Leonidas Oikonomou]] as a Doctor to treat his sick Wife, [[Caesonia Oikonomou]].","x":-100,"y":480,"width":287,"height":117},
		{"id":"ed61ce4cdb4fe8ab","type":"text","text":"[[Dr. Sanguis]] diagnoses [[Caesonia Oikonomou]] with a Terminal Illness, which [[Leonidas Oikonomou]] refuses to accept- insisting on her treatment.\n\nKnowing that's not possible, [[Dr. Sanguis]] switches to providing her with hospice care. [[Dr. Sanguis]] attempts to make it clear the treatment isn't going to save her life, but [[Leonidas Oikonomou]] is more focused on the fact that she should stay alive than what [[Dr. Sanguis]] is telling him.\n","x":-100,"y":640,"width":287,"height":524},
		{"id":"94e759df42ca4794","type":"text","text":"[[Dr. Sanguis]], being left with no career, and seeing that everything they have is at an imminent risk of being lost, tracks down [[Leonidas Oikonomou]] in a desperate fury, and kills him.\n\n[[Dr. Sanguis]] gains Aetherborne status.","x":-100,"y":1500,"width":287,"height":308},
		{"id":"f1d486c4ba01c1c4","type":"text","text":"[[Marcus Caecor]] visits home to find both of his parents dead.","x":965,"y":5847,"width":335,"height":73},
		{"id":"f839a96900e1c91e","type":"text","text":"[[Marcus Caecor]] kills [[Marcus Murder Victim]].","x":965,"y":5714,"width":335,"height":60},
		{"id":"2ea6c801e8016b56","type":"text","text":"\n[[Nishi Tsukanda]] freaks out that [[Sakishi Yamanaka]] is going to die for real, but [[Lynia]] figures out that she may be able to save it by splitting the soul in two, and potentially later recombine it.\n\nShe does so, successfully stabilizing it. However the use of soul magic breaks her (come back to this later to update), and she attacks Nishi.\n\n[[Nishi Tsukanda]] kills [[Lynia]] in self defense.\n\n","x":1620,"y":-2820,"width":360,"height":396},
		{"id":"baedc916d6e16ce8","type":"text","text":"[[Nishi Tsukanda]] develops the original two [[Docent]]s to contain the two halves of [[Sakishi Yamanaka]]'s soul.","x":1620,"y":-2360,"width":360,"height":118},
		{"id":"510ee3cb5c1cc35a","type":"text","text":"[[Valerius Oikonomou]] dies on a job.","x":-2200,"y":-1580,"width":250,"height":79},
		{"id":"1c333c6c13702a8a","type":"text","text":"[[Marcus Caecor|Marcus Oikonomou]] essentially enters a rebellious teen phase, and disappears from his family's eyes for awhile.\n\nDuring this time he meets [[TBN Caecor]], a human near his age who he falls in love with.\n\n[[TBN Caecor]] teaches Marcus to play guitar, and the two end up making music together. Marcus eventually moves in with [[TBN Caecor]]","x":-2200,"y":-1400,"width":250,"height":540},
		{"id":"625790c823c8901a","type":"text","text":"[[Marcus Caecor|Marcus Oikonomou]]","x":-1740,"y":-1529,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"a369717ff3bdea1c","type":"text","text":"[[Nishi Tsukanda]] starts to live separately from the Yamanakas","x":1620,"y":-4660,"width":360,"height":80},
		{"id":"0c8f67e658f7d7b4","type":"text","text":"Yamanaka family stuff to be added later (need to think about how the metalworks came to be)","x":2160,"y":-4660,"width":360,"height":87},
		{"id":"e06e1669f3329b8c","type":"text","text":"","x":1680,"y":-840,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"10b10afefbe725a2","type":"text","text":"[[Dr. Sanguis]] is hired by [[Suuna Yamanaka]] ","x":-81,"y":2040,"width":250,"height":58},
		{"id":"cc760656f4484937","type":"text","text":"[[Caesonia Oikonomou]] dies, and [[Leonidas Oikonomou]] loses it on [[Dr. Sanguis]], accusing them of murder. Through his use of money and bribes, he ultimately manages to get [[Dr. Sanguis]] stripped of their licence.","x":-100,"y":1200,"width":287,"height":267},
		{"id":"ac304e1031b066b3","type":"text","text":"[[Suuna Yamanaka]] builds [[Keina Yamanaka]].","x":2340,"y":-2468,"width":304,"height":88},
		{"id":"7687f802d3cf175b","type":"text","text":"[[Nishi Tsukanda]] eventually visits [[Suuna Yamanaka]], seeing him for the first time since [[Sakishi Yamanaka]]'s Death. He meets a young [[Keina Yamanaka]], and gifts Suuna the docent with Sakishi's soul, but avoids addressing the whole murder thing during the visit.\n\nDuring this visit Nishi finds out that Suuna is running a metalworks, and just kinda. slips him a buisness card like hey if you ever wanna work together i could probably use you as a supplier for some stuff","x":1840,"y":-1940,"width":337,"height":483},
		{"id":"ac8bc31ac9df3141","type":"text","text":"A bunch of people ([[Aetherborne]]s) in [[Mitsilveln 1]] go missing. The [[Royal Academy of Mitsilveln]] is hit hard by this, as a bunch of students and teachers go missing.","x":4160,"y":-364,"width":250,"height":264},
		{"id":"f7215f048b73540e","type":"text","text":"[[Stigandr]] shows up at [[Aeberos Altha]]'s house with [[Altha]] in hand, and gives it to him. [[Aeberos Altha]] visits the academy and bonds with the sword, suggesting to him that his mother is dead.","x":4160,"y":-40,"width":250,"height":300},
		{"id":"fe67bf7da1f6d42c","type":"text","text":"[[Nishi Tsukanda]] becomes interested in tech, and eventually meets [[Lynia]], who he befriends.","x":1620,"y":-4506,"width":360,"height":88},
		{"id":"1a525de4c87e5317","type":"text","text":"[[Lynia]] reveals her studies on [[Soul Magic]] to [[Nishi Tsukanda]].\n\n[[Nishi Tsukanda]] has the idea of making something that allows souls to interface with technology, even if they aren't connected to a body, and the two begin to work on the prototype for [[Soul Urns]].","x":1620,"y":-4380,"width":360,"height":284},
		{"id":"5e21411945377891","type":"text","text":"At some point the Yamanakas visit [[Nishi Tsukanda]], and [[Sakishi Yamanaka]] finds Nishi's notes on the soul urns. [[Sakishi Yamanaka]] immediately freaks out, causing him to get into an argument with [[Nishi Tsukanda]].\n\n[[Nishi Tsukanda]] refuses to swear off soul magic permanently, and [[Sakishi Yamanaka]] attempts to kill him to prevent him from causing future harm.\n\nWhile attempting to defend himself, [[Nishi Tsukanda]] accidentally shatters [[Sakishi Yamanaka]]'s [[Power Crystal]], effectively killing him.\n\n[[Suuna Yamanaka]], having heard the argument, checks on the two of them only to find [[Nishi Tsukanda]] standing over [[Sakishi Yamanaka]]'s corpse. He runs off.\n\n[[Nishi Tsukanda]] panics, and traps [[Sakishi Yamanaka]]'s soul in a prototype [[Soul Urn]]. ","x":1620,"y":-4000,"width":360,"height":716},
		{"id":"89eafb69658a06d7","type":"text","text":"[[Nishi Tsukanda]] brings [[Sakishi Yamanaka]]'s soul to [[Lynia]]. \n\n[[Lynia]] is concerned by the fact that the prototype wasn't ready to hold a soul, and studies the filled prototype to figure out the flaws that need to be corrected.\n\nShe figures out that the protoype is flawed enough where it's actively fucking up the soul.\n","x":1620,"y":-3220,"width":360,"height":324},
		{"id":"228760eaf9017e6f","type":"text","text":"[[Aeberos Altha]] is made an Aetherborne.","x":4160,"y":340,"width":250,"height":79},
		{"id":"a583a1138c0be605","type":"text","text":"# CALAMITY","x":4160,"y":-513,"width":250,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"8782ff28ea82b0ba","type":"text","text":"[[Orobi's Ex-Friend]] attacks [[Orobi Tsukanda]] outside of Orobi's apartment building, and abandons his unconscious body. ","x":1680,"y":4580,"width":250,"height":220},
		{"id":"52475d63228007e1","type":"text","text":"During a Vigilante mission where he passes by Tsukanda's appartment, [[Keina Yamanaka]] spots Orobi's unconscious body.\n\nAfter the mission, he goes to check on him. He carries Orobi to his appartment, and calls [[Nishi Tsukanda]] to tell him that he found Orobi.","x":1680,"y":4880,"width":250,"height":440},
		{"id":"ed916785a382fedb","type":"text","text":"[[Nishi Tsukanda]] helps [[Orobi Tsukanda]] slowly recover from his injuries.","x":1680,"y":5400,"width":250,"height":117},
		{"id":"4719a26bddcec30e","type":"text","text":"[[LOCKJAW's Brother]] starts working for [[Yamanaka Metalworks]].\n","x":1997,"y":2025,"width":326,"height":88},
		{"id":"342b6ed9832ea85d","type":"text","text":"[[Erdan Ren Arkhain-Keay]] is born","x":4160,"y":-740,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"18a1d23be7f77dc2","type":"text","text":"[[LOCKJAW's Brother]] befriends [[Keina Yamanaka]]","x":1997,"y":2184,"width":326,"height":60},
		{"id":"da54d78ffe485a55","type":"text","text":"Equipment falls on [[LOCKJAW's Brother]]. The situation is dealt with improperly, and he develops reperfusion syndrome.","x":1997,"y":2304,"width":326,"height":148},
		{"id":"0506d48ea328c477","type":"text","text":"[[Dr. Sanguis]] does what they can, but [[LOCKJAW's Brother]] ultimately passes away. ","x":1997,"y":2584,"width":326,"height":88},
		{"id":"24d13fb22263a74a","type":"text","text":"To prevent [[LOCKJAW's Brother]]'s soul from being shredded, it is trapped in a [[Soul Urn]]. [[Nishi Tsukanda]] connects it to a [[Docent]], which is given to [[Keina Yamanaka]].","x":1997,"y":2764,"width":326,"height":177},
		{"id":"88ff02aa0dc75288","type":"text","text":"[[Keina Yamanaka]] starts operating an automated section of [[Yamanaka Metalworks]] on his own as a mechanic.","x":1997,"y":3030,"width":326,"height":147},
		{"id":"d2b1e48c8c149ae2","type":"text","text":"[[Orobi Tsukanda]] decides to learn to fight, and eventually starts pursuing it as a career?","x":1680,"y":5640,"width":250,"height":160},
		{"id":"fef4163d8e4b7add","type":"text","text":"[[Orobi's Ex-Friend]] 'befriends' [[Orobi Tsukanda]]","x":1680,"y":4400,"width":250,"height":100},
		{"id":"47fffaa134587096","type":"file","file":"Images/Memes/char.jpg","x":2020,"y":4580,"width":395,"height":222}
	],
